# Abhishek Kumar — Portfolio

Static site. No build step — open `index.html` directly, or deploy as-is.

## Structure
```
index.html                 → main page (hero, projects, experience, achievements, about, contact)
projects/goanmart.html     → GoanMart case study (flagship, interactive architecture diagram)
projects/ablespace.html    → AbleSpace case study
projects/ecotrack.html     → EcoTrack case study
css/style.css              → design system (tokens at the top)
js/main.js                 → nav, scroll-spy, reveal animations, mobile menu, architecture diagram
resume.pdf                 → your uploaded resume (linked from nav + hero + contact)
404.html, robots.txt, sitemap.xml
```

## Before you publish — fill these in
Search the codebase for the items below; everything else is already wired from your resume.

1. **Live URLs** — GoanMart links to `https://goanmart.in` (from memory of past chats). Confirm AbleSpace and EcoTrack live URLs if they have public deployments — right now their "Code" buttons point to your GitHub profile since no specific repo/deploy URL was provided.
2. **Repo links** — all "GitHub" / "Source" buttons point to `github.com/Abhishek180-Kumar` (your profile). Swap in the specific repo URLs for GoanMart, AbleSpace and EcoTrack if you want direct deep-links.
3. **Screenshots** — every project visual is a clearly-labeled placeholder ("Project screenshot — add..."). Drop real screenshots into `assets/` and swap the `.shot-placeholder` div for an `<img>` in `index.html` and the three case-study pages.
4. **Domain** — `canonical` and Open Graph tags assume `https://abhishek-kumar.dev`. Update to your real domain once you pick one.

## Deploy
Fastest path: drag the whole folder into [Vercel](https://vercel.com/new) or [Netlify Drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop) — zero config needed for a static site. Or push to GitHub and enable GitHub Pages.

## Notes
- Dark, engineering-lab design system — near-black surface, one amber signal accent, a muted teal reserved only for "live" status indicators.
- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion`, keyboard focus states, and is responsive down to 320px.
- No fabricated numbers, users, or stats — every figure on the page traces back to your resume.
